# DEV environment - copy to .env.mcp.dev and fill in. Never commit the real file.
# DEV is a `script`-type environment: no IDE registers it, only scripts/triage.sh starts the MCP server.
# The server is always the NATIVE BINARY here (never Docker):
#   go install github.com/grafana/mcp-grafana/cmd/mcp-grafana@latest   (or a GitHub release binary)
MCP_GRAFANA_BIN=/usr/local/bin/mcp-grafana
# The corporate Grafana that has DEV's Loki as a datasource (reachable from your machine / VPN).
GRAFANA_URL=https://grafana.dev.example.internal
# Viewer service account token for THAT Grafana, scoped to the DEV Loki datasource (ask the Grafana admins).
# Preferred: fetch it at start time from your key management tool, so nothing sits on disk:
GRAFANA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN_CMD="vault kv get -field=token secret/ai-triage/dev"
# Fallback: static token (only if no key management tool is available)
# GRAFANA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=glsa_xxx
# Optional, corporate network:
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.internal:8080
# NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,.example.internal
# SSL_CERT_FILE=/path/to/corporate-ca.pem
